MacADTPro @PROJECT_VERSION_MAJOR@.@PROJECT_VERSION_MINOR@
===============

MacADTPro is a native application for transferring Apple II disk images from
a classic Macintosh with the ADTPro 2.1.0 Wide protocol. It requires a
68020-or-newer Macintosh running System 7.0 or later.

Quick start
-----------

1. Put disk images in a folder named "disks" beside MacADTPro. The application
   creates this folder automatically when it first starts.
2. Open File > Preferences and select the Macintosh serial port, transfer
   speed, and cable type.
3. Click Connect, then use Send or Receive in the ADTPro client on the Apple II.

Supported images are ProDOS-order .po files and DOS-order .dsk or .do files.
The Macintosh and Apple II must use the same baud rate.

The Bootstrap menu can load the bundled ADTPro 2.1.0 client into Apple II
memory. Follow the instructions shown by MacADTPro before clicking Send.

